\begin_layout Subsection
Useful R packages
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
To use all Bio7 functions ( for editor formating,
 knitr documents,
 markdown documents,
 spatial analysis and import,
 export of spatial data) some R packages are recommended and required to install.You can install all packages e.g.
 with a R script available in the R-Shell view context menu of Bio7 (Packages->Install_Default_R_Packages)
\end_layout

\begin_layout Subsubsection
R packages Linux specific:
 
\begin_inset CommandInset label
LatexCommand label
name "subsec:R-packages-Linux"

\end_inset


\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
For Linux there are no binaries available.
 For the compilation of the R packages the Linux packages g++ and gfortran have to be installed (if not available by default!).
 For the compilation of the rgdal package in addition you need the Linux packages:
 gdal,
 libgdal-dev,
 libproj-dev.
 If you would like to install the spatstat package,
 too,
 you need:
 libblas-dev,liblapack
\end_layout

